<title>JAPAN: Bank of Yokohama reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Bank of Yokohama reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Yokohama Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	    43.51	   207.96</p>
<p>  Bad loans			137.08	    73.44</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	 181.28	   183.97</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients   12.02	    12.04</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	  373.89	   477.41</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
